# The Python tool of `make lint`, yamllint, pinned. lint-requirements.txt, beside this file, pins
# every package it pulls in, with the SHA-256 of each of its files on PyPI, and make installs from
# it. uv writes it from this file. To change a pin, change it here, then run, with uv:
#
#     uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes \
#         --custom-compile-command 'uv pip compile, as .github/lint-requirements.in says' \
#         .github/lint-requirements.in -o .github/lint-requirements.txt
#
# uv keeps the other pins of lint-requirements.txt where they fit, so that a new release of a
# package it pulls in changes no finding. --universal resolves for each Python from 3.12, so the
# file serves CI's Python and ws's alike.
yamllint==1.38.0
